ubhead">Explore</div><ol class=3D"indent"><li style=3D"list-style-type: non=
e;"><p><b>Survey target application: </b>Due to the number of NoSQL databas=
es available and the numerous language/API combinations of each, the advers=
ary must first survey the target application to learn what technologies are=
 being leveraged and how they interact with user-driven data.</p><div class=
=3D"indent"><table width=3D"98%" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" border=
=3D"0" style=3D"margin-top:15px; margin-bottom:10px"><tbody><tr><th class=
=3D"darker">Techniques</th></tr><tr><td valign=3D"top">Determine the techno=
logy stack leveraged by the target application, such as the application ser=
ver, drivers, frameworks, APIs, and databases being utilized. </td></tr><tr=
><td valign=3D"top">Identify areas of the application that interact with us=
er input and may be involved with NoSQL queries. </td></tr></tbody></table>=
</div></li></ol><div class=3D"subhead">Experiment</div><ol class=3D"indent"=
><li style=3D""><p><b>Identify user-controllable input susceptible to injec=
tion: </b>After identifying the technology stack being used and where user-=
driven input is leveraged, determine the user-controllable input susceptibl=
e to injection such as authentication or search forms. For each user-contro=
llable input that the adversary suspects is vulnerable to NoSQL injection, =
attempt to inject characters or keywords that have special meaning in the g=
iven NoSQL database or language (e.g., "$ne" for MongoDB or "$exists" for P=
HP/MongoDB), or JavaScript that can be executed within the application. The=
 goal is to create a NoSQL query with an invalid syntax.</p><div class=3D"i=
ndent"><table width=3D"98%" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" border=3D"0=
" style=3D"margin-top:15px; margin-bottom:10px"><tbody><tr><th class=3D"dar=
ker">Techniques</th></tr><tr><td valign=3D"top">Use web browser to inject i=
nput through text fields or through HTTP GET parameters. </td></tr><tr><td =
valign=3D"top">Use a web application debugging tool such as Tamper Data, Ta=
mperIE, WebScarab,etc. to modify HTTP POST parameters, hidden fields, non-f=
reeform fields, etc. </td></tr><tr><td valign=3D"top">Use network-level pac=
ket injection tools such as netcat to inject input </td></tr><tr><td valign=
=3D"top">Use modified client (modified by reverse engineering) to inject in=
put. </td></tr></tbody></table></div></li><li style=3D""><p><b>Experiment w=
ith NoSQL Injection vulnerabilities: </b>After determining that a given inp=
ut is vulnerable to NoSQL Injection, hypothesize what the underlying query =
looks like. Iteratively try to add logic to the query to extract informatio=
n from the database, modify/delete information in the database, or execute =
commands on the server.</p><div class=3D"indent"><table width=3D"98%" cellp=
adding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" border=3D"0" style=3D"margin-top:15px; margi=
n-bottom:10px"><tbody><tr><th class=3D"darker">Techniques</th></tr><tr><td =
valign=3D"top">Use public resources such as OWASP's "Testing for NoSQL Inje=
ction" [<a href=3D"https://capec.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html#REF-66=
8">REF-668</a>] or Null Sweep's "NoSQL Injection Cheatsheet" [<a href=3D"ht=
tps://capec.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html#REF-669">REF-669</a>] and t=
ry different approaches for adding logic to NoSQL queries. </td></tr><tr><t=
d valign=3D"top">Iteratively add logic to the NoSQL query and use detailed =
error messages from the server to debug the query. </td></tr><tr><td valign=
=3D"top">Attempt an HTTP Parameter Pollution attack to replace language-spe=
cific keywords, such as "where" within PHP [<a href=3D"https://capec.mitre.=
org/data/definitions/460.html">CAPEC-460</a>]. </td></tr></tbody></table></=
div></li></ol><div class=3D"subhead">Exploit</div><ol class=3D"indent"><li =
style=3D"list-style-type: none;"><p><b>Exploit NoSQL Injection vulnerabilit=
y: </b>After refining and adding various logic to NoSQL queries, craft and =
execute the underlying NoSQL query that will be used to attack the target s=
ystem.</p><div class=3D"indent"><table width=3D"98%" cellpadding=3D"0" cell=
spacing=3D"0" border=3D"0" style=3D"margin-top:15px; margin-bottom:10px"><t=
body><tr><th class=3D"darker">Techniques</th></tr><tr><td valign=3D"top">Cr=
aft and Execute underlying NoSQL query </td></tr></tbody></table></div></li=
></ol></div></div></div></div></div><div id=3D"Prerequisites"><div class=3D=
